    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0400" n="386" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p1/pg386"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">845.00/9–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in India</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Donovan</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New Delhi</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-13T16:00:00+05:30">September 13,
                            1948—4 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>830. Razvi, Hyderabad Agent-General, advises me Mir Laik Ali<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d307-f1"/> telephoned him at 10:30 a. m. today stating that GOI
                    troops had entered Hyderabad from Sholapur, Bezwada, and Chanda. Hyderabad
                    troops have clashed with Indian Army at Naldrug in Hyderabad state near
                    Sholapur.</p>
                <p>Razvi expects to leave for Hyderabad under safe conduct within next 48 hours.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 830. Department pass London.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donovan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="1" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>Prime Minister of Hyderabad.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
